    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d239-a1">

                <pb facs="0272" n="258" sameAs="frus:frus1944v06/pg258"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure 1]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nelson Agenda</hi>
                </head>
                <p rendition="#flush">
                    <hi rendition="#italic">A. Defeat of Japan</hi>
                </p>
                <p>Unified military leadership</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">
                    <hi rendition="#italic">B. Unified China</hi>
                </p>
                <p>Concrete evidence of leadership in China</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">
                    <hi rendition="#italic">C. Work out practical relationship with Russia</hi>
                </p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Unification of agencies in China through Minister of Supply or War
                        Production Board, to cover <list>
                            <item>Production</item>
                            <item>Communications</item>
                            <item>Purchases</item>
                        </list>
                    </item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Work out supply of civilian goods for China to increase military
                        production and to improve morale of civilian population. This involves <list>
                            <item>Allotment of more C–46 planes for CNAC<anchor n="27"
                                    xml:id="d239-f1"/>
                            </item>
                            <item>Construction and improvement of airports</item>
                            <item>Utilization of trained pilots</item>
                        </list>
                    </item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>Postwar plans <list>
                            <item>Public ownership <list>
                                    <item>Power</item>
                                    <item>Communications</item>
                                </list>
                            </item>
                            <item>Private ownership <list>
                                    <item>Textiles</item>
                                    <item>Iron &amp; Steel</item>
                                    <item>Shoes and Leather</item>
                                    <item>Consumer goods</item>
                                    <item>Agricultural implements</item>
                                    <item>Chemicals</item>
                                    <item>Oils</item>
                                    <item>Forest Products and Building Materials</item>
                                    <item>Machinery</item>
                                </list>
                            </item>
                        </list>
                    </item>
                    <label>4.</label>
                    <item>Appointment of mission by President to come to China to work out details
                        of postwar plans.</item>
                    <label>5.</label>
                    <item>Development of Exports to the U. S.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><dateline rendition="#float-left">(Received by Ambassador from Mr. Nelson,
                            <date calendar="gregorian" when="1944-09-13">September 13,
                        1944</date>).</dateline></closer>
            </div>
